Feed cards now show a DELETE button (admin-only) right alongside
LIKE/SAVE/SHARE, so admins can remove a listing directly from the feed
without opening it first, matching the explicit request.

Super admin's delete-user modal now asks which scope to delete:
'Just this user account' (existing behavior, unchanged) or 'This user
AND all their records' (new — calls the backend's cascade=true option
added in the matching backend commit), with a clear explanation of
what each choice does and a success message summarizing what was
actually removed.

Also upgraded two remaining native alert()/silent-catch spots in the
car detail page to the existing toast system for consistency — comment
delete failures and car delete failures now show a real message
instead of either a blocking native alert or nothing at all.
